(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2608241650-cleanup-residue-holding-the-content")
  (:adr/title "Rename residue is usually safe to delete — except when it is the only thing holding the content")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-24")
  (:adr/related "adr-2608124400-shallow-clone-ancestry adr-2608136000-six-questions adr-2607211600-shallow-retired")
  (:adr/body
  "## What this session did

A `git cleanup conflict` pass over the superproject and its west children.

**Superproject, now clean.** Three local branches (`funny-davinci-28973e`,
`gallant-proskuriakova-d438bd`, `nostalgic-carson-73d9f1`) were each 0 ahead of
`origin/main`; two registered worktrees and one orphan removed; no stashes.
The orphan `.claude/worktrees/grammar-tmlanguage` had a gitdir pointing into a
cloud session's path that does not exist on this machine, and all six of its
differing blobs are in `kotoba-lang/grammar`'s object DB as the state before
`5e03de5` and `edbedb4`.

**Landed.** Two merges:

- `com-junkawasaki/root` 07228f52 — the observatory projection, 19h newer than
  main and never committed. `shionome` moved off `:known-broken` (exit 143 at
  615s, now 636ms); `hirameki` now meets the idempotent expectation it was
  recorded against.
- `net-kotobase/control-plane` PR #495 / 14ccccd0 — `GET /api/auth/me`, a
  credential-free projection letting an agent confirm which tenant/actor/
  permissions its credential resolved to. Eight tracked files, none of whose
  content was anywhere in history. Verified on the current base: bundle-manifest
  OK (committed bundle matches its 120 source inputs), 467 tests / 2288
  assertions / 0 failures, and `check-test-registry` confirms `kotobase.core-test`
  is among the 53 namespaces that actually run.

## The finding: three residues, three different right answers

All three were classified `:path-override-leftover` by `west-orphan-audit`, and
in all three the successor was west-registered with the leftover's `main`
contained in it. The usual conclusion — residue, delete — was right twice and
wrong once, and the difference was not visible in the classification.

| leftover | successor state | right answer |
|---|---|---|
| `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp` (13 GB, shallow) | full history at the pin | delete |
| `kotoba-lang/compiler` (184 MB) | clean at the pin | delete |
| `etzhayyim/software.diaspora.nodeinfo` (181 MB) | **0 annex objects, 26,406 broken symlinks** | **keep** |

The third is a git-annex dataset whose content lives at the dead path:
25,970 objects in the leftover, zero in the registered successor. The
west-registered checkout cannot read its own data; the unregistered one can.
A 30-key custody sample (`whereis`, no network) reads here 30/30, b2 30/30,
kotobase 2/30 — so B2 has it and this is not the only copy, but deleting takes
most keys from two copies to one, against the numcopies guidance in
`large-binary-datalad`.

**Containment is a claim about history. It is not a claim about the bytes.**
`merge-base --is-ancestor` answers whether commits are reachable, and for a
dataset that stores its payload outside the commit graph that question is
answered `yes` while the payload sits somewhere else entirely. Before deleting
a leftover, ask what it holds that is not in its history: annex objects,
untracked output, an annex branch ahead of the shared ref.

## Two near-misses worth keeping

**A truncated listing reports absence.** `repos/kotoba-lang/amu/branches`
returns 100 rows of 222, and the truncated page said 6 of 10 branches were
local-only — i.e. at risk. Direct per-ref lookup showed all 10 pushed at the
same tip. A capped listing and a real absence have the same shape, which is
ADR-2608136000's first question appearing in an API rather than in a gate.

**A clean 0/40 usually means the file moved.** Content-containment scoring on
`kotoba-lang/compiler`'s branches read 0/40 added lines present for
`component_{core,composition}.clj`. The files do not exist on main at all —
removed by `adda825 refactor: consume the extracted repos instead of owning
them`. Scoring a missing file yields the same number as scoring an unlanded
change.

## Un-landed work reunited with its live path, not committed

Twice the residue and the successor held two halves of the same thing:

- `ongakuka`: the successor had each render's `<name>_input_params.json` and
  none of the audio; the residue had the audio and none of the params. The 12
  `.wav`/`.mp3` were moved to the live path, where `.gitignore` has excluded
  `artifacts/ *.wav *.mp3` since 2026-07-17 — the repo's own stated policy.
- `nodeinfo`: 377 files existed nowhere else — 375 `raw/nodes/*.json` and the
  fetch reports for offsets 61 and 62, continuing past the successor's range.
  Moved to the live path. Four `raw/peers/*.json` were not moved: those paths
  are annex-tracked and the leftover's copies are a newer crawl with different
  sizes and sha256 from the keys the symlinks name, so overwriting them is an
  annex operation, not a file move.

## Open, for the owner

1. `control-plane/scripts/migrate_dataverse_gftd.rb` — a 195-line one-off
   migration and the only `.rb` in the repo. Committing it introduces a script
   host ADR-2607173000 excludes; deleting it destroys work. Archived, left in
   place.
2. `cloud-itonami/ongakuka` main tracks 12 audio files (12.8 MB) in paths
   `.gitignore` had already excluded for eight days when a `cleanup: land
   untracked WIP` pass added them. The API write path does not consult
   `.gitignore`, and each file is ~1.5 MB, just under the 2 MB per-file skip.
   The residue gate added 2026-08-05 would catch it now.
3. `kotoba-lang/amu` has 10 pushed branches with no PR, ADR 0052-0060. All nine
   ADRs are on main (now at 0271) and the sources they touch are gone. PRs
   would be unmergeable against deleted paths.
4. `software.diaspora.nodeinfo` needs `datalad get` in the successor from b2,
   or an objects move plus a git-annex branch merge. Then the leftover retires.
5. The 377 rescued nodeinfo files are untracked at the live path and still need
   `datalad save` and a B2 copy.

## Measured

Zero shallow checkouts across 4,288 (was one — `ai-gftd-apps-gftdcojp`, which
the SessionStart hook named; removal was the fix, not unshallow, because the
slug redirects to a repo west already carries with full history). ~12 GB
reclaimed. `west-orphan-audit` exit 0. Path-override leftovers 4 -> 2.
Archive at `.git/stash-archive-2026-08-24/`, 12 MB, 10 classified entries.")))
